  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The alcohols (3) and (2) are both 3<sup>o</sup>, but alcohol (3) gives a more substituted alkene. Alcohol&nbsp;(4) and (1) are both 2<sup>o</sup>, but alcohol (4) can give a more substituted alkene and alcohol (5) is 1<sup>o</sup>. Rate of dehydration of alcohols with concentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>&nbsp;follows the order 3<sup>o</sup> &gt; 2<sup>o</sup> &gt; 1<sup>o</sup>.",
